# iran-mcp-router

When the user asks for something from the Iranian web (prices, flights,
food, doctors, stocks, classifieds, maps, news, ...), do NOT guess which
MCP server handles it and do NOT read the whole iran-mcp catalog.

1. Run the router first (one cheap deterministic call):
   `python3 scripts/router_cli.py "<the task>"`  (repo: iran-mcp-router)
   or call the `route_task` tool if the iran-mcp-router MCP server is configured.
2. It returns ranked candidates: `server_id`, `suggested_tool`,
   `install` (e.g. `uvx tgju-mcp`), `repo`, and `reason`.
3. Install the chosen server and call its `suggested_tool`.
   All routed servers are read-only and need no sign-in.

Queries work in Persian (نیم‌فاصله and ي/ك variants are normalized) and English.
The router is deterministic: same query, same ranking.
